{{Quote|The [[Void]] is a paradise. I can wield my power here without shame. Unfortunately, I didn't have [[Professor X/Cassandra Nova Birthed|Charles Xavier]] to teach me temperence.|Cassandra Nova to [[Deadpool]] and [[Wolverine]]|Deadpool & Wolverine}}
'''Cassandra Nova Xavier''' was an Omega-level [[Mutants|mutant]] and the twin sister of [[Professor X/Cassandra Nova Birthed|Charles Xavier]]. Being banished to the [[Void]] by the [[Time Variance Authority]], Nova took a liking to it and gained permission to run her operations there as she pleased, building an armed [[Cassandra Nova's Henchmen|community of survivors]]. Nova came into conflict with freshly pruned [[Deadpool]] and [[Wolverine]] who were trying to get home, while Nova had no intention to let them out. When the [[Resistance]] successfully disrupted her operations, Nova was betrayed and almost killed by [[Pyro]] but Deadpool and Wolverine helped her survive, so she got them out of the Void. Realizing that the TVA and [[Paradox]] broke their agreement, Nova followed them out of the Void, intending to use the [[Time Ripper]] and eradicate all the realities in the multiverse besides the Void. Her plan failed, and Nova was atomized by the energy of the Time Ripper when Deadpool and Wolverine overloaded it.

==Biography==
===Early Life===
====Banished to the Void====
{{Quote|[[Time Variance Authority|They]] sent me [[Void|here]] before I could walk. And you know, that's the best thing that ever happened to me. I love it here.|Cassandra Nova to [[Deadpool]] and [[Wolverine]]|Deadpool & Wolverine}}
Cassandra Nova was born as the twin sister of [[Professor X/Cassandra Nova Birthed|Charles Xavier]], trying to strangle him with her umbilical cord while they both were still in a womb. Before Cassandra learned how to walk,{{Ref|DW}} Xavier psychically killed Nova as he became one of the most powerful mutants of all time. This led to her getting discovered by the [[Time Variance Authority]]<ref name="Psychic Death">[https://www.tiktok.com/@marvel/video/7397167312396176670?_r=1&_t=8oXgfjLALsY Marvel Entertainment on TikTok - July 29, 2024]</ref> and sent to the [[Void]] by them. Unlike most of the Void inhabitants, Nova took a liking to her new place of living, as she could use her extraordinary powers without any restraint or shame.{{Ref|DW}} She rapidly became one of the most formidable entities in the Void, with the only comparable power being the more beastly [[Alioth]], while building a [[Cassandra Nova's Henchmen|community]] of other Void survivors based in [[Giant-Man/Pruned Giant-Man|Giant-Man]]'s [[Cassandra Nova's Compound|corpse]].{{Ref|DW}} She began finding inhabitants of the Void to psychically torture using her mutant abilities.<ref name="Psychic Death"/>

Nova's reign over the Void was not without pushback, as some survivors refused to be her slaves and formed the [[Resistance]] to overthrow her. However, each and every attempt to take Nova down only resulted in loss and casualties, with Nova personally killing [[Magneto]] and destroying his [[Magneto's Helmet|helmet]] that allowed the wearer to withstand her psychic powers. 

Nova's cruelty wasn't just limited to members of the Resistance as she often killed stray [[Glossary#Variants|Variants]] who were unwilling to bend to her will. This included a version of her twin, [[Hub:Charles Xavier|Charles Xavier]], who she killed before taking his [[Charles Xavier's Wheelchair|wheelchair]] for herself. She also killed a [[Doctor Strange/Pruned Doctor Strange|Doctor Strange]] who was present in the Void before she skinned him and wore his skin for several days. She also obtained this Strange's [[Time Stone|Time]] and [[Reality Stone]]-infused [[Sling Ring]] that gave her the ability to leave the Void if she wished. She was approached by [[Paradox]] from the TVA, who offered to let her deal with the variants in the Void however she wanted so that TVA could keep Nova at bay.{{Ref|DW}}

===[[Preservation of Earth-10005|Conflict with Deadpool & Wolverine]]===
====New Arrivals====
[[File:Cassandra Nova in the Void.jpg|{{AltFloat}}|Nova steps out to greet her new prisoners]]
{{Quote|But I'm not like the rest of you. Except maybe the Wolverine. Now, we could be truly terrifying together."<br>"You're that scary, huh?|Cassandra Nova and [[Wolverine]]|Deadpool & Wolverine}}
[[Pyro]] and [[Toad]] returned from their hunt, and had successfully captured [[Human Torch/Void Analyzing Fantastic Four|Human Torch]], as well as [[Deadpool]] and [[Wolverine]], so Nova came out to speak with them. After getting up from [[Charles Xavier's Wheelchair]], Nova remarked about this was the first [[Hub:Logan|Wolverine]] she had encountered in the [[Void]], knowing him as one of [[Professor X/Cassandra Nova Birthed|Professor X]]'s [[X-Men/Mutant Genocide|X-Men]]. [[Deadpool]] asked how she knew Professor X, so she explained her past to them as his twin sister.
[[File:Deadpool & Wolverine Purpose (17).png|{{AltFloat}}|Nova introduced to [[Deadpool]] and [[Wolverine]]]]
Nova was amused by Deadpool and Wolverine, so she untied them and then turned her attention to Human Torch, who she had been trying to capture for years. Deadpool interrupted, revealing the foul things Human Torch had said about Nova, although Human Torch tried to deny it as Deadpool persisted. Nova listened to the insults about her, and decided to kill Human Torch, brutally ripping his skin off his body with telekinesis. Nova witnessed [[Alioth]] approaching the [[Cassandra Nova's Compound|compound]] as Deadpool tried to explain that he was trying to save his world.
[[File:Cassandra Nova (D&W).jpg|{{AltFloat}}|Nova explains how she ended up in the [[Void]]]]
Nova was doubtful of Deadpool's ability to save his own world, which she sensed was something he was sensitive about. Wolverine enquired about the wheelchair, so Nova told him how she would encounter Variants of her brother occasionally. Nova then commented on how she was similar to Wolverine in regard to how dangerous they were, and she elaborated on how she ended up in the Void, expressing how much she loved her life. Wolverine went to attack Nova, but she gleefully stopped him in place and buried him in the ground with her powers.
[[File:Cassandra Nova Crew.jpg|{{AltFloat}}|Nova refuses to help [[Deadpool]] return home]]
Deadpool pleaded that he only wanted to get back home, which Nova could organize but she did not want to. Nova used her powers to force her hand through Deadpool's head to access his memories. Discovering a memory of Deadpool and [[Vanessa Carlysle]] breaking up, Nova manipulated Carlysle's words to make her say that he would never matter, knowing that was Deadpool's biggest insecurity. Wolverine snuck up behind Nova and stabbed her, but it had no effect and she knocked him away. As Alioth neared, Nova retreated to let Deadpool and Wolverine die, but they managed to escape.{{Ref|DW}}

====[[Attack on Cassandra Nova's Compound|Dethroned]]====
[[File:Cassandra Nova Looks Out.jpg|{{AltFloat}}|Nova witnessing the [[Resistance]]'s assault]]
{{Quote|[[Professor X/Mutant Genocide|He]] would have loved you, too. If he knew about you. If he knew where you were, he would have torn a hole in the fucking universe to bring you home."<br>"[[Void|This]] is my home."<br>"Well then at least us save [[Deadpool|his]].|[[Wolverine]] and Cassandra Nova|Deadpool & Wolverine}} 
The next day, Nova witnessed her [[Cassandra Nova's Compound|compound]] fall under attack by the [[Resistance]], who were joined by [[Deadpool]] and [[Wolverine]]. Nova stared at Deadpool, and gave a look of amusement at the heroes' attempt to fight back against her. Nova walked away, leaving her [[Cassandra Nova's Henchmen|henchmen]] to deal with the Resistance.
[[File:Deadpool & Wolverine Trailer (117).png|{{AltFloat}}|Nova controlling [[Wolverine]] telekinetically]]
Nova sat down and waited for Deadpool and Wolverine to make their way to her, exclaiming that she was fine with them [[Escape from Cassandra Nova's Compound|escaping]], but thought them willingly returning was foolish. Deadpool once again pleaded that he needed to return home, but Nova rejected his request, offering either death or enslavement. Nova threw Deadpool around the room, knocking him out, allowing her and Wolverine to talk. However, Wolverine attacked her, so she forced his claws into the floor, restraining him.
[[File:Cassandra Nova looks at Wolverine.png|{{AltFloat}}|Nova forcefully entering [[Wolverine]]'s mind]]
Not at risk of being attacked, Nova continued talking to Wolverine, pointing out how interesting she found him, noting that [[Hub:Wade Wilson|Deadpools]] were very common in the [[Void]]. Nova then entered her finger into Wolverine's head and accessed his mind. Nova was surprised to find the pain that Wolverine was living with behind all of his anger he projected. The two talked about how he abandoned the [[X-Men/Mutant Genocide|X-Men]] before they were all murdered, which led to him going on a killing spree.

Sensing his vulnerability, Nova attempted to sway Wolverine, telling him that he could be whoever he truely was in the Void. Wolverine told her that he just wanted to be free from the pain, so Nova assured him she could silence all of the voices in his head that drove his guilt. In a rare moment of compassion, Nova comforted Wolverine, but it turned out Wolverine was just keeping her distracted so that Deadpool could affix [[Juggernaut]]'s [[Juggernaut's Helmet|helmet]] to her head, disabling her powers.

Deadpool demanded that Nova return them home, but she just laughed, knowing that they would need to remove the helmet in order for her to do that. However, Nova evilly declared that if they did take off the helmet she would immediately kill them, remarking that she would boil their brains on an atomic level while masturbating to the {{WPS|Enya}} box set. Realizing they were in a stalemate, Deadpool and Wolverine argued over which one of them would kill Nova, only for her to be shot repeatedly by [[Pyro]].

With her healing capabilities prevented, Nova would die soon from the gunshot wounds, so Deadpool once more asked if they could trust her not to kill them if he took the helmet off, but Nova remained fixated on killing them instantly. Despite this, Wolverine demanded that the helmet be removed, telling Nova that although he wanted to kill her, [[Professor X/Mutant Genocide|Professor X]] would not want him to let her die. Once the helmet was removed, Nova pretended to go to kill Deadpool, but did not, having been influenced by Wolverine's admiration for her brother.

Wolverine insisted to Nova that had Professor X known about her existence he would have stopped to no end to find a way to bring her back home. Nova was satisfied with the Void as her home, so Wolverine asked her to help them save Deadpool's. Nova equipped the [[Sling Ring]] she took from [[Doctor Strange/Pruned Doctor Strange|Doctor Strange]] and used it to open a [[Inter-Dimensional Portal|portal]] to Deadpool's universe. Although she decided to help them, Nova informed them that within seconds [[Alioth]] would devour them, and she watched as Deadpool and Wolverine ran through the portal.{{Ref|DW}}

====[[Attack on Earth-10005|Attacking the Multiverse]]====
{{Quote|You know, the funny thing is I was happy in the [[Void]]. You sent your trash to me, [[Alioth]] and I cleaned it up, everyone was happy. And you had to go and piss on my side of the fence. And so now the fence must come down. I'm going to use your little [[Time Ripper]] and I'm going to destroy [[Anchor Being Wolverine|this universe]] and the next, and the next, and the next until all that's left is the Void. And I get to play God.|Cassandra Nova to [[Mr. Paradox]]|Deadpool & Wolverine}}
Nova stood over the unconscious [[Pyro]], and when he woke up, she wanted to know why he had shot her. She attempted to stick her fingers in his head, but Pyro decided just to tell her, being repulsed by her method of interrogation. Nova learned that [[Mr. Paradox]] made a deal with Pyro to kill Nova in order to be freed from the [[Void]]. Realizing that Paradox had broken their agreement, Nova decided to enact revenge against him.

Using the [[Sling Ring]], Nova traveled to [[Deadpool]]'s [[Anchor Being Wolverine|reality]], where she killed Pyro right in front of Deadpool, [[Wolverine]] and [[Mr. Paradox]]. Nova confronted Paradox for trying to have her killed, and stuck her fingers in his head. Accessing Paradox's mind, Nova discovered the [[Time Ripper]], which Deadpool told her they were planning to destroy. However, Nova wanted to use it, so she launched Deadpool and Wolverine away, leaving just her and Paradox, who she told her plan to destroy the [[Multiverse]] because he broke their arrangement.
[[File:Deadpool & Wolverine Final Trailer (17).png|{{AltFloat}}|Nova attempts to destroy [[Deadpool]]'s [[Anchor Being Wolverine|reality]]]]
Nova dragged Paradox to the [[TVA]]'s station in the subway station, telling him that she summoned the [[Deadpool Corps]] to stop them from being interrupted, and she forced him to activate the the Time Ripper. Nova approached the Time Ripper and began to use it to destroy Deadpool's universe. Right as she was about to completely obliterate the reality, the process started to be undone by Deadpool and Wolverine. Nova tried to resist, but they were able to overload the Time Ripper, which atomized Nova, killing her.{{Ref|DW}}

==Personality==
{{Quote|If I take this [[Juggernaut's Helmet|helmet]] off, do you promise you won't kill us?"<br>"I promise I will kill you first thing."<br>"Oh, why are you like this!"<br>"I wish I knew.|[[Deadpool]] and Cassandra Nova|Deadpool & Wolverine}}
Cassandra Nova is characterized by a blend of mischievousness, courtesy, and unpredictability. Johnny Storm describes her as dangerously insane, with megalomaniacal and psychopathic tendencies. Cold and manipulative, she thrives on making life difficult for others. Her early denial of existence and upbringing in a lawless, chaotic environment have instilled in her a deep-seated malice and resentment towards the TVA. Unlike Professor X’s measured demeanor, she is playful and carefree in speech, but her actions are deeply malevolent. Notably, she killed the Human Torch after he insulted her, remained indifferent to her subordinates' fates, and feeds innocent survivors in the Void to Alioth to keep her safe. These actions in cold-blood reflect her fundamental neglect in the lives of others. She also exhibited streaks of insanity, as she laughed manically when she was stabbed in the back by Wolverine during their first encounter, and even when her life was at risk, being shot by Pyro multiple times while her powers were nullified by Juggernaut's helmet, she still laughed and threatened to kill Deadpool and Wolverine even if they saved her. Cassandra's mischievousness was exhibited in her use of telekinesis in which she not only subdues her enemies, but plays with them by controlling their body parts and torturing them both physically and mentally. Cassandra hated the fact that her mind-reading abilities have to be activated by direct physical contact with the enthralled's brain, having to reaching beneath the skin to do so, while Charles Xavier could do so with a thought alone. She had developed a hatred towards this skill as she was forced to read into the darkest secrets of others, some that profoundly disgust her. Although she speaks in a reassuring tone, this should not be mistaken as friendliness as she hides her violent inclinations behind her harmless front.

Cassandra's chaotic upbringing has led her to seek stability and control. She exhibited authoritarian tendencies, was highly intolerant of betrayal, and responded to threats to the stability of her rule with extreme cruelty. After years of management, she had become the ''de facto'' leader of the Void, with her crew of pruned villains and the Deadpool Corps working for her. Her vow to destroy all universes, leaving only the Void for her rule, reflects her vengefulness and lack of empathy, particularly in response to Pyro and Paradox's betrayal. Her sadistic nature is evident in her violent actions, such as peeling off Storm's skin, killing a variant of Doctor Strange and wearing his skin for days, and violently breaking Pyro's neck. After realizing Paradox's betrayal of their mutual agreement, Cassandra immediately decided to take over the Time Ripper and destroy all timelines as retribution for Paradox's actions.

Despite her cruelty, Cassandra displays a vulnerable side. When entering Wolverine's mind, she appears genuinely moved by his pain and loss, attempting to convince him to join her by promising to alleviate his suffering and offer him a place in the Void. This is because Cassandra herself also had been through a similar situation. Having grown up alone without the love of family, she found that she could do whatever she wanted in the Void, where she sees as a paradise of freedom. Hence she suggested this Wolverine, who also lost everything, to embrace his beastly self. Cassandra also harbors an inferiority complex and sibling rivalry towards Professor X, having killed several of his variants and stolen one of their wheelchairs. She believes Professor X from her reality never pursued her out of indifference, though he was unaware of her existence. Later, when Wolverine saves her life and appeals to her heart, stating that Professor X would have done everything possible to bring her home had he known of her, Cassandra agrees to return them to their universe, reflecting that despite all she has done to the variants of her twin brother, she craves this sibling love deep down.

==Powers and Abilities==
===Powers===
{{Quote|You led an Omega-level [[Mutants|mutant]] to [[Earth-10005|this timeline]].|[[Hunter B-15]] to [[Deadpool]] and [[Wolverine]]|Deadpool & Wolverine}}
*'''Mutant Physiology''': Cassandra Nova was an Omega-level [[Mutants|mutant]] as well as the twin sister of the powerful telepath [[Professor X/Cassandra Nova Birthed|Charles Xavier]]. Hence, she possesses powers similar to Xavier's.
**'''Psionics''': Cassandra's mutation granted her a wide array of psionic abilities. As an Omega-level Mutant, her psionic powers are exceptionally potent, enabling her to endure in the hostile environment of the [[Void]] and establish a [[Cassandra Nova's Henchmen|community]] of loyal survivors.
***'''Telekinesis''': Cassandra can move things with her mind, as shown when she telekinetically controlled [[Wolverine]]'s body and easily skinned [[Human Torch/Void Analyzing Fantastic Four|Johnny Storm]], killing him instantly.
****'''Telekinetic Regeneration''': Due to her advanced telekinetic capabilities, Cassandra can endure and regenerate from fatal injuries with ease. This ability allowed her to survive most encounters with [[Resistance]] [[:Category:Resistance Members|members]] who attempted to defeat her. However, this regeneration ability is limited, as she loses this ability, along with her other telekinetic-based ones, when she is under influence of a mind-nullifying object, such as [[Magneto]]’s [[Magneto's Helmet|helmet]] or [[Juggernaut]]’s.
****'''Telekinetic Blast:''' Cassandra can project waves of telekinetic energy to impulse, hit and destroy multiple objects and/or people. With a snap of her fingers, she was able to create a shock wave of telekinetic energy to send Deadpool and Wolverine several meters away.
****'''Intangibility''': Cassandra can pass through solid matter by passing her atoms through the spaces between the atoms of the object through which she is moving. In this way, she and the object through which she is passing can temporarily merge without interacting, and each is unharmed once Cassandra has finished passing through the object. She can make her fingers penetrate her targets' heads to read their minds, as demonstrated with [[Deadpool]] and Wolverine. Additionally, she can merge this ability with her telekinesis to break a target's neck, as she did with [[Pyro]].
***'''Tactile Telepathy''': Unlike her twin brother, Cassandra needs physical contact with her target to activate her telepathy.
****'''Memory Walking''': Cassandra can enter and interact with another person's memories. She uses this power to extract information, as demonstrated when she delved into Wolverine’s memories to understand the root of his rage. She also employed this ability on Pyro and [[Paradox]] to learn about the [[Time Ripper]] and how to utilize it.
***'''Mental Manipulation''': ''To be added''
*'''[[Magic]]''': Once she killed an [[Doctor Strange/Pruned Doctor Strange|alternate]] [[Doctor Strange]] who was banished to the Void, Cassandra Nova kept his [[Sling Ring]] which granted her several [[magic]] powers, including the ability to conjure [[Inter-Dimensional Portal]]s with ease.
**'''[[Magic#Eldritch Magic|Eldritch Magic]]''': ''To be added''
***'''Portal Creation''': Cassandra had a Sling Ring, able to create sustained portals between two points. Using the portals, she was able to transport others to another dimension and later retrieve them.

